   920	    *,
     1	"""Process-global Inductor GEMM backends, claimed for one game per process.
     2	
     3	Compiled Kaggriculture regions lower GEMMs to cuBLAS only (``"ATEN"``) on the
     4	probed torch/triton/driver stack; Isaiah's Orbit models keep the backends they
     5	find. ``torch._inductor.config`` is process-global and Inductor reads it when a
     6	compiled callable first runs or recompiles, not at ``torch.compile``, so every
     7	public compile entry point (``configure_model_compile`` and each model's
     8	``compile_transformer_trunk``) claims the setting for its game before compiling,
